  "version": "1.7.3",
  "changelog": "Fixes the freeze when opening a big building. (1) Opening Elizabeth Baptist Church (and any other large building) no longer freezes the editor: finding which street a building faces used to re-measure every road in the zone for every edge of the building \u2014 over 3 million measurements for that one church. It now measures only the roads near the building and gets the same answer in a fraction of a second (checked identical on 2,260 buildings across all seven zones). Everything else is unchanged from 1.7.2.",
